            <ArticleTitle>[A primigravida with abdominal pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A2219</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 35-year-old primigravida presented with abdominal pain and urine retention due to an incarcerated uterus. The diagnosis was based on clinical symptoms, ultrasound and MRI. At a gestational age of 34 weeks and 3 days the patient delivered by caesarean section.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
